<file path=".github/instructions/backend.instructions.md">
  1: ---
  2: applyTo: "apps/backend/**"
  3: ---
  4: 
  5: # Backend Development Instructions
  6: 
  7: ## ✅ Phase 1 Progress
  8: 
  9: - OAuth authentication, paper management, collections, and workspaces are production-ready.
 10: - AI summarization + multi-provider insights shipped (Gemini primary, OpenAI fallback).
 11: - Dashboard restructure delivered with role-based routing, admin tools, and workspace refinements.
 12: 
 13: Keep new work aligned with these shipped milestones and follow the standards below.
 14: 
 15: ## 🚀 Production-Ready Improvements
 16: 
 17: ### Security & Performance Standards
 18: 
 19: - **Debug Logging Control**: Auth middleware conditionally logs only in development (`NODE_ENV !== "production"`)
 20: - **Type Safety**: Replace all `any` types with proper interfaces (use `AuthenticatedRequest` for authenticated routes)
 21: - **Rate Limiting**: Apply paper-specific rate limiters (`paperUploadLimiter`, `paperListLimiter`, `paperOperationLimiter`) to all endpoints
 22: - **Database Performance**: Add composite indexes for hot query paths (e.g., `Paper` queries by `uploaderId + workspaceId`)
 23: - **Performance Monitoring**: Use `performanceMonitor` middleware to track response times and add `X-Response-Time` headers
 24: 
 25: ### Error Handling Standards
 26: 
 27: - **Backend Error Classes**: Create feature-specific error classes (e.g., `PaperError`) extending `ApiError` for consistent error responses
 28: - **Standardized Error Format**: All errors follow `{ success: false, message: string, statusCode: number, errorCode?: string, details?: object }`
 29: - **Health Check Endpoints**: Comprehensive monitoring at `/api/health/*` (basic, detailed, live, ready probes)
 30: 
 31: ### Production Pitfalls to Avoid
 32: 
 33: - ❌ Logging debug info in production (always check `NODE_ENV`)
 34: - ❌ Using `any` types (use proper interfaces like `AuthenticatedRequest`)
 35: - ❌ Missing rate limiting on upload/mutation endpoints
 36: - ❌ Missing performance monitoring on critical paths
 37: - ❌ Not handling BigInt serialization in JSON (cast to integer in SQL)
 38: 
 39: ## Architecture & Structure
 40: 
 41: - **Structure**: Feature modules under `src/app/modules` (controller, service, routes, validation schemas)
 42: - **Routes**: Register in `src/app/routes` only. No ad-hoc route registration elsewhere
 43: - **Controllers**: Thin. Business logic belongs in services
 44: - **Services**: Use Prisma client from shared singleton. Handle transactions explicitly when needed
 45: - **Validation**: Zod for request bodies, params, queries. Reject early on failure
 46: 
 47: ## Database Operations - Prisma Client vs Raw SQL Decision Tree
 48: 
 49: **PREFER Prisma Client when:**
 50: 
 51: - Simple CRUD operations
 52: - Standard relationships and joins
 53: - OAuth account management (CRITICAL: use upsert patterns)
 54: - User management and basic queries
 55: 
 56: **Use `$queryRaw` / `$executeRaw` when:**
 57: 
 58: - Complex joins not ergonomic in Prisma Client
 59: - Performance-critical read paths with explicit SQL + indexes
 60: - Complex aggregations or window functions
 61: - Bulk operations that need optimization
 62: 
 63: ### Implementation Standards
 64: 
 65: ```typescript
 66: // ✅ CORRECT: Prisma Client for standard CRUD
 67: const users = await prisma.user.findMany({
 68:   where: { isDeleted: false },
 69:   orderBy: { createdAt: "desc" },
 70:   skip,
 71:   take: limit,
 72: });
 73: 
 74: // ✅ CORRECT: Use $queryRaw for complex/performance-critical queries
 75: const users = await prisma.$queryRaw<User[]>`
 76:   SELECT id, email, name, "createdAt"
 77:   FROM "User"
 78:   WHERE "isDeleted" = false
 79:   ORDER BY "createdAt" DESC
 80:   LIMIT ${limit} OFFSET ${skip}
 81: `;
 82: ```
 83: 
 84: ### Security & Performance
 85: 
 86: - **SQL Injection Prevention**: Use template literals: `WHERE email = ${email}`
 87: - **Type Safety**: Use `prisma.$queryRaw<Type[]>` for proper typing (never `any[]`)
 88: - **Field Selection**: Select only required fields, avoid `SELECT *`
 89: - **Pagination**: Use `LIMIT ${limit} OFFSET ${skip}` for efficient pagination
 90: 
 91: ## Authentication & Security
 92: 
 93: - **OAuth Account Management**: ALWAYS use standard Prisma upsert for OAuth accounts
 94: - **Raw Query Warning**: Do NOT change OAuth account creation to raw queries - causes unique constraint errors (P2002)
 95: - **Error Handling**: All auth methods must use try/catch with ApiError for consistent error responses
 96: - **JWT**: Use JWT access + refresh. Use `auth` middleware for protected endpoints
 97: - **CORS**: Use `FRONTEND_URL` env; default `http://localhost:3000` in dev
 98: 
 99: ## Testing & Quality
100: 
101: - **Testing**: Add unit tests for non-trivial service logic; integration tests for new routes
102: - **Critical Features**: Authentication flows require comprehensive test coverage
103: - **Errors**: Throw `ApiError(status, message)`; avoid returning partial successes silently
104: - **Logging**: Avoid console noise. Use structured logs for important events
105: 
106: ## Prisma & Database
107: 
108: - **Prisma**: After modifying schema run migrations then `yarn db:generate` (includes TypedSQL)
109: - **Raw SQL**: Keep raw SQL in `prisma/sql` (one statement per file)
110: - **TypedSQL**: Import from `@prisma/client/sql`; execute with `$queryRawTyped` or `$queryRaw`
111: - **pgvector**: Only run similarity queries if `USE_PGVECTOR=true`. Ensure extension exists before deploying usage
112: - **Pagination**: Use provided pagination helper; never return unbounded lists
113: 
114: ## Environment & Configuration
115: 
116: - **Config**: Centralized in `src/config/index.ts` (loads `.env`)
117: - **CORS**: Respect `FRONTEND_URL` for CORS; default API port is 5000
118: - **Secrets**: Store secrets in `.env` only; never log secrets
119: - **Feature Flags**: Use `FEATURE_*` variables for gating backend features
120: 
121: ## Code Quality
122: 
123: - **Lint/Typecheck**: Run `yarn lint` and `yarn type-check` on every change
124: - **TypeScript**: Avoid implicit `any`, unused exports
125: - **Dependencies**: Prefer standard libs and already-installed packages. Justify new deps in PR
126: - **Do not use npm**: Use Yarn v4 workspaces
127: 
128: ## Roadmap Discipline
129: 
130: - Follow `Roadmap.md` sequence strictly: complete Phase 1 items (auth ✅, uploads, collections, basic search) before Phase 2, then Phase 3
131: - If a feature request is out-of-phase, document it and add minimal scaffolding only if needed to unblock Phase 1
132: 
133: ## Phase Overview
134: 
135: - **Phase 1**: Auth ✅, profile, file uploads (S3 integrated), paper/collection CRUD, basic search
136: - **Phase 2**: Collaboration (roles, shared collections/workspaces), citation graph/formatting, improved UI
137: - **Phase 3**: Billing (Stripe), admin tooling, external integrations, QA and launch
</file>

