  1: ---
  2: applyTo: "apps/frontend/**"
  3: ---
  4: 
  5: # Frontend Development Instructions
  6: 
  7: ## ✅ Phase 1 Progress
  8: 
  9: - Auth flows, modern dashboard shell, paper/collection/workspace tooling are live.
 10: - AI chat + summarization UI launched (Gemini-first with OpenAI fallback).
 11: - Role-scoped dashboard routing and admin overview UX refresh delivered.
 12: 
 13: Keep new UI consistent with these delivered experiences and the standards below.
 14: 
 15: ## 🚀 Advanced Error Handling
 16: 
 17: ### RTK Query Enhancement with Retry Logic
 18: 
 19: - **Enhanced API Slice**: Use retry configuration and error transformation with `retry(baseQuery, { maxRetries: 3 })`
 20: - **Error Classification**: Network errors (auto-retry), client errors 4xx (manual fix), server errors 5xx (auto-retry)
 21: - **Smart Retry Logic**: Auto-retry on network/server errors, skip retry on client errors
 22: 
 23: ### Sonner Toast Integration
 24: 
 25: - **Use ToastProvider Functions**: Never import `toast` directly from Sonner
 26: - **Proper Usage**: Use `showErrorToast`, `showSuccessToast` from `@/components/providers/ToastProvider`
 27: - **Error Toast Best Practices**: Use `showApiErrorToast()` from `@/lib/errorHandling` - respects network error retry logic
 28: 
 29: ### Custom Error Handling Hooks
 30: 
 31: - **Generic Error Handler**: `useErrorHandler(error, options)` for any error with automatic toast/logging
 32: - **Query Error Handler**: `useQueryErrorHandler(queryResult, options)` with refetch capability
 33: - **Mutation Error Handler**: `useMutationErrorHandler(mutationResult, retryFunction, options)` with retry logic
 34: 
 35: ### Error Handling Standards
 36: 
 37: - **Smart Retry**: Auto-retry on network/server errors, manual retry for client errors
 38: - **Consistent Messaging**: Use error utilities for consistent user-friendly error messages
 39: - **Development Logging**: Detailed error logs only in development environment
 40: - **Toast Integration**: Leverage existing Sonner setup with theme support and positioning
 41: 
 42: ## Core Development Standards
 43: 
 44: - **Next.js App Router**: Prefer Server Components; add "use client" only where interactivity/state is needed
 45: - **Dev Server**: Runs on port 3000. Backend CORS should allow `http://localhost:3000` in dev
 46: - **State/Data**: RTK Query + React Redux. Set `baseUrl: "/api"`; attach auth headers in `prepareHeaders` when available
 47: - **Forms**: React Hook Form + Zod. Validate on server too for trust boundaries
 48: - **Auth**: NextAuth (JWT). Keep tokens server-only; never expose secrets; wrap app with provided `NextAuthProvider` and `ReduxProvider`
 49: - **UI**: Tailwind + ShadCN. Keep primitives in `components/ui`; compose variants with `class-variance-authority`
 50: - **Performance**: Use `next/image` and `next/font`; stream with Suspense where useful; minimize client JS
 51: - **Virtualization**: Use `react-window` for large data lists (papers, collections, search results)
 52: - **Sanitization**: Use `sanitize-html` for all user-generated HTML content before rendering
 53: - **SEO**: Use Metadata API; add `app/sitemap.ts` and `app/robots.ts` when routes stabilize; consider JSON-LD for key pages
 54: - **Error States**: Provide loading / empty / error UI for each data fetch
 55: - **Accessibility**: Maintain focus states, labels, keyboard navigation
 56: 
 57: ## UI/UX Guidelines
 58: 
 59: - **Consult `docs/UI_DESIGN.md` FIRST** before creating new pages or major UI changes
 60: - Follow established authentication patterns for consistent user experience
 61: - Use feature flags for incomplete features as documented in the UI design blueprint
 62: - Maintain accessibility standards: keyboard navigation, focus states, ARIA labels
 63: - Follow component taxonomy:
 64:   - `components/auth/` - Authentication components ✅
 65:   - `components/layout/` - Navigation and layout components
 66:   - `components/ui/` - ShadCN primitives ✅
 67:   - `components/customUI/` - Custom components
 68: 
 69: ## Design System Standards
 70: 
 71: - **Colors**: Use OKLCH color system with existing success, warning, info variants
 72: - **Typography**: Use Typography component with established heading scales
 73: - **Spacing**: Use max-w-[1440px] container width and consistent padding scales
 74: - **Animations**: Use existing hover effects (lift, scale, glow) and transitions
 75: 
 76: ## Authentication Patterns ✅
 77: 
 78: - Login/register pages follow established design with proper form validation
 79: - OAuth integration with Google/GitHub providers working
 80: - Error handling and loading states implemented
 81: - Responsive design tested across breakpoints
 82: - Password strength indicators and form validation in place
 83: 
 84: ## Code Quality
 85: 
 86: - **Lint/Typecheck**: Run `yarn lint` and `yarn type-check` on every change
 87: - **TypeScript**: No implicit `any`, no unused exports
 88: - **Performance**: Implement lazy loading, React.memo for expensive components
 89: - **Accessibility**: WCAG 2.1 AA compliance, proper ARIA labels and roles
 90: - **No Secrets**: Never expose private keys or tokens in client code
 91: - **Do not use npm**: Use Yarn v4 workspaces
 92: 
 93: ## Environment & Configuration
 94: 
 95: - **Environment**: Always check both envs before changing behavior: `apps/frontend/.env.local` and `apps/backend/.env`
 96: - **CORS**: Ensure `FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000` in backend `.env` for CORS in dev; do not commit secrets
 97: - **Feature Flags**: Use feature flags from env: `NEXT_PUBLIC_FEATURE_*` variables for gating UI elements
 98: 
 99: ## Roadmap Discipline
100: 
101: - Follow `Roadmap.md` and work sequentially: Phase 1 (MVP) → Phase 2 (Advanced) → Phase 3 (Premium/Integrations)
102: - If a requested change is out-of-phase, implement only if it unblocks the current phase, otherwise note as "Next steps"
103: 
104: ## Phase Overview
105: 
106: - **Phase 1**: Auth ✅, profile, uploads, collections, basic search/UI. Keep UI pragmatic and fast
107: - **Phase 2**: Collaboration (shared collections, workspaces), citation graph/formatting, enhanced UI
108: - **Phase 3**: Billing (Stripe), admin panel, external APIs, QA & launch
109: 
110: ## Frontend Best Practices
111: 
112: ### Routing, Data, and Rendering
113: 
114: - Prefer Server Components; use Client Components only when interaction/state is needed
115: - Use App Router layouts for shared chrome; colocation of route handlers where appropriate
116: - Fetch on the server when possible; leverage Next.js caching (ISR) for marketing pages
117: - Use `revalidate`/tag-based invalidation (`revalidateTag`, `revalidatePath`) for content updates
118: 
119: ### SEO & Metadata
120: 
121: - Use the Metadata API in `layout.tsx`/`page.tsx` (`title`, `description`, `openGraph`, `twitter`, `alternates.canonical`, `robots`)
122: - Implement `generateMetadata` for dynamic routes (paper, collection, user)
123: - Add `app/sitemap.ts` and `app/robots.ts`; include dynamic entries for papers/collections
124: - Include structured data (JSON-LD) for Organization, WebSite, BreadcrumbList, Article/ScholarlyArticle
125: 
126: ### Performance & UX
127: 
128: - Use `next/image` and `next/font` (self-host fonts); preconnect/prefetch critical resources
129: - Minimize client JS; split by route/segment; use streaming/Suspense and skeletons for perceived speed
130: - Debounce searches; paginate or infinite-scroll large lists; avoid N+1 client fetches
131: - Avoid heavy client-only UI libs when headless + Tailwind suffices
132: 
133: ### Security
134: 
135: - JWT best practices: short-lived access tokens, refresh rotation, revoke on logout
136: - HTTP security headers (helmet), rate limiting, input validation, file type/size limits
137: - Regular dependency audits; pin critical packages; monitor CVEs
</file>

