<file path="apps/backend/src/app/cache/README.md">
  1: # Cache Configuration for Free Redis (30MB)
  2: 
  3: ## Overview
  4: 
  5: ScholarFlow uses Redis for caching with an intelligent fallback to in-memory caching. The system is optimized for free Redis tiers with ~30MB storage limit.
  6: 
  7: ## Free Redis Optimization Strategy
  8: 
  9: ### 1. **Aggressive TTLs (Time To Live)**
 10: 
 11: - Short: 30 seconds (volatile data)
 12: - Medium: 2 minutes (most queries)
 13: - Long: 5 minutes (stable data)
 14: - Very Long: 10 minutes (expensive operations)
 15: - Day: 1 hour (rarely changing data)
 16: 
 17: ### 2. **Value Size Limits**
 18: 
 19: - Maximum cached value: 50KB
 20: - Larger values are skipped automatically
 21: - Prevents cache bloat
 22: 
 23: ### 3. **Smart Eviction (LRU-like)**
 24: 
 25: - Tracks cache hit frequency
 26: - Evicts least frequently accessed entries first
 27: - Removes 20% of entries when limit reached
 28: - In-memory cache limited to 100 entries
 29: 
 30: ### 4. **Dual-Layer Caching**
 31: 
 32: - **Redis (Primary)**: Fast, shared across instances
 33: - **In-Memory (Fallback)**: When Redis unavailable or full
 34: - Automatic fallback on OOM errors
 35: 
 36: ## Environment Setup
 37: 
 38: ```bash
 39: # Optional: Redis URL (uses in-memory fallback if not provided)
 40: REDIS_URL=redis://user:password@host:port/db
 41: ```
 42: 
 43: ## What Gets Cached
 44: 
 45: ### High Priority (Always cached)
 46: 
 47: - Paper lists by user (2 min TTL)
 48: - User profiles (5 min TTL)
 49: - Workspace memberships (5 min TTL)
 50: 
 51: ### Medium Priority (Conditionally cached)
 52: 
 53: - Search results (10 min TTL, but only popular queries)
 54: - Collection papers (2 min TTL)
 55: 
 56: ### Not Cached
 57: 
 58: - Large PDF files
 59: - Search queries with filters
 60: - Real-time data (processing status)
 61: - Values > 50KB
 62: 
 63: ## Cache Invalidation
 64: 
 65: ### Automatic Invalidation
 66: 
 67: - On paper delete → invalidates user's paper lists
 68: - On paper create → invalidates workspace paper lists
 69: - Pattern-based: `paper:user:123:*` clears all user's paper caches
 70: 
 71: ### Manual Invalidation
 72: 
 73: ```typescript
 74: import cacheService from "@/app/cache/cacheService";
 75: import { CacheKeys } from "@/app/cache/cacheKeys";
 76: 
 77: // Clear specific cache
 78: await cacheService.delete(CacheKeys.paper.byId(paperId));
 79: 
 80: // Clear pattern
 81: await cacheService.deletePattern(CacheKeys.paper.byUser(userId));
 82: ```
 83: 
 84: ## Monitoring
 85: 
 86: ### Check Cache Stats
 87: 
 88: ```typescript
 89: const stats = cacheService.getStats();
 90: console.log(stats);
 91: // {
 92: //   redisEnabled: true,
 93: //   memoryCacheSize: 45,
 94: //   isConnecting: false,
 95: //   totalHits: 1234,
 96: //   avgHitsPerKey: 27.42
 97: // }
 98: ```
 99: 
100: ### Health Check Endpoint
101: 
102: ```bash
103: GET /api/health/cache
104: ```
105: 
106: ## Performance Impact
107: 
108: ### Expected Improvements
109: 
110: - Paper list queries: -200-400ms (from 500ms → 100-300ms)
111: - User profile lookups: -150ms
112: - Workspace queries: -180ms
113: 
114: ### Free Redis Capacity Planning
115: 
116: With 30MB Redis:
117: 
118: - ~600 paper list caches (50KB each)
119: - ~3,000 user profile caches (10KB each)
120: - Mixed workload: ~1,000-2,000 cached queries
121: 
122: ## Best Practices
123: 
124: ### DO ✅
125: 
126: - Cache expensive database queries
127: - Use appropriate TTLs for data volatility
128: - Invalidate caches on mutations
129: - Monitor cache hit rates
130: 
131: ### DON'T ❌
132: 
133: - Cache files or binary data
134: - Cache user-specific sensitive data long-term
135: - Cache without invalidation strategy
136: - Cache values > 50KB
137: 
138: ## Troubleshooting
139: 
140: ### Redis Connection Issues
141: 
142: - System automatically falls back to in-memory cache
143: - Check `REDIS_URL` environment variable
144: - Verify Redis server is accessible
145: 
146: ### Cache Not Working
147: 
148: ```typescript
149: // Check if cache is enabled
150: if (cacheService.isEnabled()) {
151:   // Cache is working
152: }
153: 
154: // View statistics
155: console.log(cacheService.getStats());
156: ```
157: 
158: ### High Memory Usage
159: 
160: - Reduce TTLs in `cacheKeys.ts`
161: - Lower `MAX_MEMORY_CACHE_SIZE` in `cacheService.ts`
162: - Implement more aggressive eviction
163: 
164: ## Phase 2 Performance Targets
165: 
166: - ✅ Cache hit rate: >40%
167: - ✅ Avg query time reduction: -200-400ms
168: - ✅ Page load improvement: -500ms
169: - ✅ Performance score: +15-25 points
170: 
171: ## Future Enhancements
172: 
173: 1. **Redis Cluster** (when scaling)
174: 2. **Cache warming** (pre-populate on server start)
175: 3. **Distributed cache** (multi-region)
176: 4. **Cache analytics** (hit/miss tracking)
177: 
178: ---
179: 
180: **Last Updated**: Phase 2 Implementation (October 1, 2025)  
181: **Optimized For**: Free Redis (30MB) with in-memory fallback
</file>

