321: ## Socket-Server Environment Variables
322: 
323: File: `apps/socket-server/.env`
324: 
325: | Variable | Description | Dev Value |
326: |----------|-------------|-----------|
327: | `PORT` | WebSocket server port | `5001` |
328: | `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` | Must match the backend/frontend `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` | `openssl rand -base64 32` |
329: | `FRONTEND_URL` | CORS allowed origin (no trailing slash) | `http://localhost:3000` |
330: 
331: The socket server verifies JWT tokens on WebSocket handshake using `NEXTAUTH_SECRET`. It must match exactly what the backend and frontend use.
332: 
333: ## Dev Redirect URIs Summary
334: 
335: | Service | Provider | Callback URL |
336: |---------|----------|--------------|
337: | better-auth | Google | `http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google` |
338: | better-auth | GitHub | `http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/github` |
339: 
340: ## Dev Webhook URLs
341: 
342: | Service | Endpoint |
343: |---------|----------|
344: | Stripe | `POST http://localhost:5000/webhooks/stripe` |
345: | SSLCommerz | `POST http://localhost:5000/webhooks/sslcommerz` |
346: 
347: ## Production Notes
348: 
349: When deploying:
350: 
351: - Set `NEXTAUTH_URL` to your production domain (e.g., `https://app.scholar-flow.com`)
352: - Update OAuth redirect URIs in Google/GitHub consoles to use production URLs
353: - Use production database, S3 bucket, and Stripe live keys
354: - Restrict CORS by updating `FRONTEND_URL`
355: - Generate new, strong secrets (never reuse dev secrets in production)
356: - Store secrets in Vercel/Render dashboard, not in `.env` files
357: 
358: ## Security
359: 
360: - Never commit `.env` files (they're in `.gitignore`)
361: - Use strong secrets (32+ bytes) and rotate periodically
362: - Limit AWS IAM/S3 permissions to least privilege
363: - Validate Stripe webhook signatures (don't trust unverified payloads)
364: - Keep `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` in sync across all three apps
365: 
366: ## Troubleshooting
367: 
368: **Problem: Auth callback fails with "redirect_uri_mismatch"**
369: Cause: The OAuth provider's configured redirect URI doesn't match what the app sends.
370: Fix: Verify the callback URL in Google/GitHub console matches `http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/{provider}`.
371: 
372: **Problem: Backend won't start — "Missing NEXTAUTH_SECRET"**
373: Cause: The backend can't start without an auth secret.
374: Fix: Set `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` in `apps/backend/.env`. Even a placeholder value works for dev.
375: 
376: **Problem: CORS errors in browser console**
377: Cause: `FRONTEND_URL` in the backend doesn't match your actual frontend URL.
378: Fix: Ensure `FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000` (no trailing slash).
379: 
380: **Problem: Prisma client errors on `yarn dev:backend`**
381: Cause: Prisma client needs to be generated.
382: Fix: Run `yarn db:generate` from the repo root.
383: 
384: ## Related Docs
385: 
386: - [Setup Guide](./SETUP.md) — initial environment setup
387: - [Redis Setup](./REDIS_SETUP.md) — Redis configuration options
388: - [Database Setup](./DATABASE.md) — PostgreSQL + pgvector
389: - [Deployment Guide](./DEPLOY.md) — production env configuration
