 98: - [ ] **Sweep test** (optional, needs DB access): backdate the subscription's
 99:       `expiresAt` to >7 days ago → within the hourly sweep the role reverts
100:       to RESEARCHER and status becomes EXPIRED (or run
101:       `runSubscriptionSweep()` directly via ts-node).
102: - [ ] After downgrade: billing page shows Free + upgrade card again.
103: 
104: ## 6. Admin panel — Subscriptions & Revenue (`/dashboard/admin/subscriptions`)
105: 
106: - [ ] Loads as ADMIN; MRR / ARR / Total Revenue / Active Subscribers cards.
107: - [ ] **Trial exclusion**: a user in a 14-day trial is NOT in MRR/ARPU/
108:       Active Subscribers (trial shows only in "Subscriptions by Status").
109: - [ ] **Revenue Trend chart** renders daily bars; tooltip shows date +
110:       amount; empty state when no payments in range.
111: - [ ] Time range selector (7d/30d/90d/1y) + Refresh button work.
112: - [ ] "Payment Insights": failed count matches FAILED Payment rows;
113:       success rate = succeeded/(succeeded+failed).
114: - [ ] Top Paying Customers: one row per user, total spent excludes refunds.
115: 
116: ## 7. Admin panel — Subscribers (`/dashboard/admin/subscribers`)
117: 
118: - [ ] Table lists all subscriptions; status filter + pagination work.
119: - [ ] **Cancel at period end** (ACTIVE row) → row shows "Cancel scheduled";
120:       verify in Stripe dashboard the subscription has cancel_at_period_end.
121: - [ ] **Reactivate** → "Cancel scheduled" disappears; Stripe confirmed.
122: - [ ] **Change plan** → dialog lists active plans → switch Pro↔Team →
123:       success toast; role changes via webhook within seconds; verify the
124:       Stripe subscription's price changed.
125: - [ ] **Cancel now** → confirm dialog → subscription canceled; role reverts
126:       to RESEARCHER; "Canceled" badge; audit log entry.
127: - [ ] Audit trail: `/dashboard/admin/audit` shows `canceled_at_period_end`,
128:       `reactivated`, `plan_changed`, `canceled_now` entries.
129: 
130: ## 8. Admin panel — Payments (`/dashboard/admin/payments`)
131: 
132: - [ ] Search by email / transaction id (300ms debounce — one request per
133:       pause, not per keystroke).
134: - [ ] Refund a SUCCEEDED payment → button shows "Refunding…" spinner →
135:       success toast → row becomes REFUNDED; **money actually returned**
136:       (check Stripe dashboard → Payments → Refunds, and the customer sees
137:       the refund).
138: - [ ] Refund button hidden on REFUNDED/FAILED/PENDING rows.
139: - [ ] Page shows "This page revenue" + "Total payments".
140: - [ ] After a refund, the Subscriptions page revenue refreshes (tag
141:       invalidation) without manual reload.
142: 
143: ## 9. Admin panel — Plans (`/dashboard/admin/plans`)
144: 
145: - [ ] **New plan** dialog: create a test plan (code/name/price/interval) →
146:       card appears with interval label + short price ID.
147: - [ ] **Edit price** → a NEW Stripe price is created (check Stripe dashboard →
148:       Products → the price list shows the new amount) and the card's price
149:       ID changes; `/pricing` shows the new price after refresh.
150: - [ ] **Edit name** → Stripe product renamed (both monthly + annual variants
151:       share the product).
152: - [ ] **Checkout with edited price**: after an edit, a new user can still
153:       start checkout with the plan's new price ID (DB-driven validation) and
154:       the webhook still grants the correct role (plan-code-based mapping).
155: - [ ] Existing subscribers keep their price until renewal (reprice per-user
156:       via Subscribers → Change plan).
157: - [ ] **Deactivate/Activate** toggle → "Inactive" badge; deactivated plans
158:       vanish from `/pricing` and checkout rejects them (400 PLAN_UNAVAILABLE).
159: - [ ] **Delete** a plan without subscribers → removed (soft-delete);
160:       delete blocked for plans with ACTIVE subscribers.
161: - [ ] Creating a duplicate `code` → error toast.
162: 
163: ## 10. Admin panel — Reports (`/dashboard/admin/reports`)
164: 
165: - [ ] Generate on a FINANCIAL report → **file downloads** (CSV/JSON) — not
166:       a 404 page (this was broken).
167: - [ ] Report row status updates to READY after generation.
168: - [ ] Export content matches Payment rows (amounts in dollars, includes
169:       refunded payments with their status).
170: 
171: ## 11. Role guards & redirects
172: 
173: - [ ] As RESEARCHER/TEAM_LEAD, visiting any `/dashboard/admin/*` URL →
174:       redirected to `/dashboard` (no blank page) + access-denied toast.
175: - [ ] As ADMIN, all pages above load normally.
176: - [ ] Logged-out user hitting `/dashboard/billing` → `/login?callbackUrl=...`.
177: 
178: ## 12. Idempotency / duplicate safety (API level, optional)
179: 
180: - [ ] Replay the same webhook payload twice → second delivery skipped
181:       (WebhookEvent unique on provider+eventId).
182: - [ ] `stripe trigger charge.refunded` → processed cleanly (dashboard
183:       refunds sync to local Payment rows when the charge's invoice matches).
184: 
185: ---
186: 
187: ## Known non-issues (verified, don't retest)
188: 
189: - `invoice.parent.subscription_details.subscription` is the correct
190:   invoice→subscription link on API `2025-09-30.clover` (docs-confirmed).
191: - Amount formatting is consistent (backend dollars for analytics, cents
192:   ÷100 on payments/plans pages).
193: - Single currency (USD) is a supported scope — multi-currency is not.
194: - `TRIALING` as a subscribers filter maps to ACTIVE (no 500).
