 22: # 🅟 PRATAY — Slides 1–4 · ~2 min total
 23: 
 24: ---
 25: 
 26: ### Slide 1 — Title _(~30 sec)_
 27: 
 28: Good morning everyone.
 29: We are Team Phantom Devs.
 30: Our project is **ScholarFlow** — an AI-powered research collaboration platform.
 31: It helps researchers upload papers, get AI summaries, annotate, and collaborate — all in one place.
 32: 
 33: ---
 34: 
 35: ### Slide 2 — Problem _(~35 sec)_
 36: 
 37: Researchers today have **four big problems**.
 38: 
 39: One — they use four or more separate apps. No single place for everything.
 40: Two — no AI help. They read every paper by hand.
 41: Three — teams cannot collaborate easily.
 42: Four — existing tools cost fifty to two-fifty dollars per month. Students cannot afford this.
 43: 
 44: ScholarFlow solves all four problems — in one affordable platform.
 45: 
 46: ---
 47: 
 48: ### Slide 3 — Motivation _(~35 sec)_
 49: 
 50: Why are we building ScholarFlow?
 51: 
 52: Because we face these problems ourselves — as students.
 53: 
 54: Switching apps wastes three or more hours every week.
 55: Ninety-one percent of researchers get zero AI help.
 56: Most tools are too expensive for students.
 57: 
 58: Our goal is one unified platform — with AI, affordable pricing, and team collaboration built in.
 59: 
 60: ---
 61: 
 62: ### Slide 4 — Objectives _(~35 sec)_
 63: 
 64: ScholarFlow has five objectives.
 65: 
 66: One — one platform for all papers.
 67: Two — AI summaries, Q&A, and literature reviews.
 68: Three — automatic metadata extraction on upload.
 69: Four — shared workspaces with role-based access.
 70: Five — a free tier for students, with affordable team plans.
 71: 
 72: These five objectives guide our entire development plan.
 73: 
 74: ---
