164: ### Slide 10 — Tech Stack _(~40 sec)_
165: 
166: Our technology stack has three layers.
167: 
168: **Frontend** — Next.js 16, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Redux Toolkit, Better Auth.
169: We chose Next.js for fast server rendering and full TypeScript support.
170: 
171: **Backend** — Node.js 22, Express.js, Prisma ORM, JWT, Zod validation.
172: Express works perfectly with Prisma for type-safe database queries.
173: 
174: **Infrastructure** — PostgreSQL with pgvector, AWS S3, Redis, Stripe, Gemini 3.5 Flash, OpenAI GPT-5.5, Vercel.
175: 
176: One full-stack TypeScript monorepo — type-safe from end to end.
177: 
178: ---
179: 
180: ### Slide 11 — Architecture _(~40 sec)_
181: 
182: ScholarFlow uses a **three-tier decoupled architecture**.
183: 
184: **User layer** — researchers and students access via browser.
185: 
186: **Frontend layer** — Next.js on Vercel handles UI, auth, and state.
187: 
188: **Backend layer** — Express REST API on Railway handles all business logic.
189: 
190: The backend connects to three service groups:
