 1: # Scholar-Flow Quickstart
 2: 
 3: Get running in ~5 minutes. For detailed explanations, see [Setup Guide](./SETUP.md).
 4: 
 5: ## Prerequisites
 6: 
 7: - **Node.js 24+**, **Yarn 4.9.2+** (`corepack enable && corepack prepare yarn@4.9.2 --activate`)
 8: - **PostgreSQL 15+** with pgvector
 9: - **Git**
10: 
11: No PostgreSQL yet?
12: ```bash
13: docker run -d --name scholar-pg -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=admin -e POSTGRES_DB=scholarflow_dev -p 5432:5432 pgvector/pgvector:pg18
14: ```
15: 
16: ## Quick Commands
17: 
18: ```bash
19: # 1. Clone
20: git clone https://github.com/Atik203/Scholar-Flow.git && cd Scholar-Flow
21: 
22: # 2. Copy env templates
23: cp apps/backend/.env.example apps/backend/.env
24: cp apps/frontend/.env.example apps/frontend/.env.local
25: cp apps/socket-server/.env.example apps/socket-server/.env
26: 
27: # 3. Set DB connection (edit apps/backend/.env)
28: #    DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:admin@localhost:5432/scholarflow_dev
29: #    DIRECT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:admin@localhost:5432/scholarflow_dev
30: 
31: # 4. Install deps + generate Prisma client
32: yarn setup
33: 
34: # 5. Create tables (prompted: type "initial_setup")
35: yarn db:migrate
36: 
37: # 6. (Optional) Seed demo data
38: yarn db:seed
39: 
40: # 7. Start all dev servers
41: yarn dev:turbo
42: ```
43: 
44: ## Verify
45: 
46: ```bash
47: curl http://localhost:5000/api/health
48: # → {"status":"ok","timestamp":"..."}
49: ```
50: 
51: Open http://localhost:3000. If seeded, log in with `admin@scholarflow.com` / `password123`.
52: 
53: ## Troubleshooting
54: 
55: | Problem | Fix |
56: |---------|-----|
57: | `command not found: yarn` | `corepack enable && corepack prepare yarn@4.9.2 --activate` |
58: | `ECONNREFUSED` database | Start PostgreSQL or Docker container |
59: | `Port 3000 already in use` | `lsof -ti:3000 \| xargs kill -9` |
60: | `Cannot find module '@prisma/client'` | `yarn db:generate` |
61: 
62: ## Next Steps
63: 
64: - [Setup Guide](./SETUP.md) — detailed configuration
65: - [Development Guide](./DEVELOPMENT.md) — day-to-day workflow
66: - [Environment Variables](./ENVIRONMENT.md) — OAuth, AI, S3 setup
67: - [Database Setup](./DATABASE.md) — PostgreSQL + pgvector
68: - [Contributing Guide](../CONTRIBUTING.md) — how to contribute
</file>

