148: ## 🚀 Quick Start
149: 
150: ### Prerequisites
151: 
152: - Node.js 24+ (check with `node --version`)
153: - Yarn Berry v4.9.2+ (check with `yarn --version`)
154: - PostgreSQL 15+ with pgvector extension
155: - AWS S3 account (for file storage — optional for local dev without uploads)
156: 
157: ### Installation
158: 
159: 1. **Clone the repository**
160: 
161:    ```bash
162:    git clone https://github.com/Atik203/Scholar-Flow.git
163:    cd Scholar-Flow
164:    ```
165: 
166: 2. **Set up environment variables**
167: 
168:    ```bash
169:    # Copy environment templates
170:    cp apps/frontend/.env.example apps/frontend/.env.local
171:    cp apps/backend/.env.example apps/backend/.env
172:    cp apps/socket-server/.env.example apps/socket-server/.env
173: 
174:    # Edit the .env files with your configurations
175:    ```
176: 
177: 3. **Install dependencies, generate Prisma client, and build**
178: 
179:    ```bash
180:    yarn setup
181:    ```
182: 
183:    This runs `yarn install` followed by `prisma generate --sql` in one step.
184: 
185: 4. **Set up the database**
186: 
187:    ```bash
188:    yarn db:migrate
189:    yarn db:seed
190:    ```
191: 
192: 5. **Start development servers**
193: 
194:    ```bash
195:    yarn dev:turbo
196:    ```
197: 
198:    The application will be available at:
199:    - Frontend: [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000)
200:    - Backend: [http://localhost:5000](http://localhost:5000)
201:    - WebSocket: [http://localhost:5001](http://localhost:5001)
202: 
203: ## 🔧 Development Commands
204: 
205: ```bash
206: # Development
207: yarn dev:turbo          # Start both frontend and backend
208: yarn dev:frontend       # Start only frontend
209: yarn dev:backend        # Start only backend
