495: ## Additional Constraints from .cursor/rules/ (read-only source)
496: 
497: ### Backend Module Architecture
498: - Feature modules live under `apps/backend/src/app/modules/` with structure: controller, service, routes, validation schemas.
499: - Routes register ONLY in `apps/backend/src/app/routes` — never register ad-hoc routes elsewhere.
500: - Controllers must be thin; all business logic belongs in services.
501: - Services use Prisma client from shared singleton; handle transactions explicitly when needed.
502: - Zod for request body, param, and query validation; reject early on failure.
503: 
504: ### Database Operations
505: - **Prefer Prisma ORM** (`findMany`, `create`, `update`, `delete`, `upsert`, `count`, etc.) for new database operations — typed queries provide better type safety, refactoring support, and readability.
506: - **Keep existing `$queryRaw` / `$executeRaw` calls as-is** — do not rewrite working raw SQL unless there is a specific performance or correctness issue.
507: - **When raw SQL is needed** (pgvector similarity, complex aggregations, CTEs not supported by Prisma):
508:   - Use template literal syntax for SQL injection prevention: `WHERE email = ${email}`
509:   - Use `prisma.$queryRaw<Type[]>` for proper typing.
510:   - Select only required fields; never use `SELECT *`.
511:   - Use `LIMIT ${limit} OFFSET ${skip}` for pagination; never return unbounded lists.
512: - **EXCEPTION — OAuth operations MUST keep standard Prisma Client upsert:**
513:   - `createAccount()`, `createOrUpdateUser()`, `createOrUpdateUserWithOAuth()`
514:   - Changing these to raw queries causes P2002 unique constraint errors.
515: 
516: ### TypedSQL & Raw SQL Files
517: - Raw SQL statements live in `apps/backend/prisma/sql/` with ONE statement per file.
518: - File names must be valid JavaScript identifiers (no leading dashes) because they become generated function names.
519: - Use positional parameters `$1`, `$2` with optional `-- @param {Type} $1:name` comments.
520: - After adding/modifying SQL, run `yarn db:generate` to regenerate typed functions.
521: - Import generated functions from `@prisma/client/sql`.
522: - Execute typed queries with `prisma.$queryRawTyped(queryName(...params))` or `prisma.$queryRaw(...)`.
523: - Always apply pending migrations BEFORE running `prisma generate --sql`.
524: - Every new TypedSQL query must have at least one test verifying shape and performance assumptions.
525: - Above any raw query usage, add a comment referencing the originating `.sql` file.
526: 
527: ### Frontend Component & Design Standards
528: - Prefer Next.js Server Components; add `"use client"` ONLY when interactivity or state is required.
529: - Use `next/image` and `next/font`; stream large UI with Suspense to avoid unnecessary client bundles.
530: - Consult `docs/UI_DESIGN.md` BEFORE creating new pages or components.
531: - Component taxonomy:
532:   - `components/auth/` — Authentication related
533:   - `components/layout/` — Navigation, headers, sidebars
534:   - `components/ui/` — ShadCN primitives
535:   - `components/customUI/` — Custom components
536: - Design system: OKLCH color system, `max-w-[1440px]` container width, established Typography heading scales.
537: - Use existing hover effects (lift, scale, glow) and transitions.
538: - SEO: use Metadata API; ensure canonical URLs; plan sitemap + robots when routes stabilize.
539: - Accessibility: WCAG 2.1 AA compliance, proper ARIA labels, roles, focus states, keyboard navigation.
540: 
541: ### Sonner Toast & Error Handling Patterns
542: - Use Sonner via ToastProvider functions ONLY:
543:   - `showErrorToast`, `showSuccessToast` from `@/components/providers/ToastProvider`
544:   - `showApiErrorToast` from `@/lib/errorHandling`
545: - NEVER import `toast` directly from `sonner`.
546: - Use custom error handling hooks:
547:   - `useErrorHandler` for generic errors
548:   - `useQueryErrorHandler` for RTK Query queries
549:   - `useMutationErrorHandler` for mutations
550: - Smart retry: auto-retry on network/server errors, manual retry for client errors.
551: - Error classification: Network (retry), Client 4xx (fix required), Server 5xx (retry).
552: - All auth methods must use try/catch with `ApiError` for consistent error responses.
553: - Feature-specific error classes must extend `ApiError` with standardized format:
554:   ```typescript
555:   {
556:     success: false,
557:     message: string,
558:     statusCode: number,
559:     errorCode?: string,
560:     details?: object,
561:     timestamp: string
562:   }
563:   ```
