565: ### Production-Ready Security & Performance Standards
566: - Debug logging is allowed ONLY in development; always gate with `process.env.NODE_ENV !== "production"`.
567: - Replace all `any` types with proper interfaces (e.g., `AuthenticatedRequest`).
568: - Apply feature-specific rate limiters to all mutation endpoints, especially uploads.
569: - Use `performanceMonitor` middleware and add `X-Response-Time` headers.
570: - Health check endpoints must exist:
571:   - `/api/health` — Basic health status
572:   - `/api/health/detailed` — Full system health
573:   - `/api/health/live` — Kubernetes liveness probe
574:   - `/api/health/ready` — Kubernetes readiness probe
575: - BigInt handling: cast to integer in SQL for JSON serialization to avoid issues.
576: - Memory monitoring: track heap usage and memory thresholds in health checks.
577: 
578: ### pgvector Detailed Rules
579: - Only run similarity queries if `USE_PGVECTOR=true`.
580: - `PaperChunk.embedding` column type is `vector`; migrations manage any transition from JSON fallback.
581: - Use a service helper to format float arrays into vector literals (`[x,y,z]`).
582: - Similarity operators: `<->` (L2), `<=>` (cosine), `<#>` (negative inner product). Align index operator class with chosen operator.
583: - Create IVF index (`ivfflat`) only after sufficient data volume; document chosen `lists` parameter.
584: - Limit result sets (e.g., `LIMIT 10`); avoid full vector scans.
585: - Guard against mismatched dimensionality; validate embedding array length before insert.
586: - Add round-trip test (insert + similarity query) when modifying embedding logic.
587: 
588: ### Auth Specifics
589: - Frontend authentication state is managed via Redux Toolkit (in addition to NextAuth session).
590: - OAuth account creation MUST use standard Prisma upsert pattern; do NOT convert to raw SQL.
591: - Password strength indicators on register forms.
592: - Auth guards for protected routes.
593: - All auth functions must have JSDoc comments.
594: - Authentication-related code requires minimum 90% test coverage.
595: - Comprehensive integration tests required for all auth endpoints and flows.
596: 
597: ### Role-Based Access Control (Phase 5+)
598: - Use the `requireRole(role)` factory from `apps/backend/src/app/middleware/requireRole.ts` for new RBAC routes. Convenience wrappers: `requireTeamLead`, `requireAdmin`.
599: - Apply the middleware AFTER `authMiddleware` in the route chain (RBAC needs an authenticated user first).
600: - Reject with `ApiError(403, "Insufficient permissions. Required: {role}, got: {userRole}")` — do not silently 200.
601: - For per-resource ownership checks (e.g. "only the workspace owner can edit settings"), perform the check inside the service via raw SQL or Prisma where/select, not in the middleware.
602: - For frontend role gating in `AppSidebar`, set `minRole: USER_ROLES.TEAM_LEAD` on the navigation item — `hasRoleAccess` handles the rest.
603: - Use `lib/auth/roles.ts` constants (`USER_ROLES.RESEARCHER`, etc.) and `hasRoleAccess(userRole, requiredRole)` — never compare role strings directly.
604: 
605: ### Email Delivery (Phase 5+)
606: - Transactional emails route through `emailService` in `apps/backend/src/app/shared/emailService.ts`.
607: - Dispatcher priority: Resend (if `RESEND_API_KEY` is set in env) → existing SMTP/Gmail transporter.
608: - Resend uses the built-in `fetch` API (`https://api.resend.com/emails`); no SDK dependency.
609: - Never add new SMTP providers without keeping Gmail as the fallback — never break local dev for users without the env var.
610: - New email templates are methods on `EmailService` (e.g. `sendTeamInvitationEmail(data)`); HTML is inlined in the method for now. If a template gets large, refactor to a `templates/` directory but keep the dispatcher call signature stable.
611: - Email send failures are logged but NEVER thrown — the main flow (invitation, etc.) must complete even if email delivery fails. Surface failures via `console.error` in dev, silent in production.
612: 
