675: 
676: ## Project Context Generation (Repomix)
677: **Repomix** is installed as a dev dependency for generating AI-friendly project snapshots.
678: 
679: ### When to regenerate
680: - After major structural changes (new directories, moved files)
681: - After adding new dependencies or build tools
682: - Before asking a new AI agent to work on the project
683: - When the project context seems stale
684: 
685: ### How to generate
686: ```bash
687: # From project root
688: npx repomix
689: # Or using the configured output
690: yarn repomix
691: ```
692: 
693: **Output file:** `repomix-output.xml` (8MB+ AI-friendly project snapshot)
694: 
695: ### What repomix includes
696: - All source code (TS, TSX, JS, JSX, CSS, SCSS, JSON, Prisma, SQL)
697: - Configuration files (package.json, tsconfig, etc.)
698: - Documentation (README, AGENTS.md, IMPLEMENTATION.md, etc.)
699: - Excludes: node_modules, images, LaTeX files, build artifacts, logs
700: 
701: ### What repomix ignores (configured in repomix.config.ts)
702: - **scholar-flow-overleaf/** — LaTeX thesis/document files (SRS, chapters, images)
703: - **response_image/** — Generated image responses
704: - **images/** — Static image assets
705: - **node_modules/**, **.yarn/** — Package dependencies
706: - **.next/**, **dist/**, **out/** — Build outputs
707: - **.git/**, **.turbo/**, **.vercel/** — VCS & deployment artifacts
708: - **.vscode/**, **.cursor/**, **.agents/**, **.figma/** — IDE & tool configs
709: - **CHANGELOG.md**, **LICENSE.md**, **CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md** — Meta docs
710: - **Logs, coverage, media files** — Non-code assets
711: 
712: ### Using repomix output with AI
713: 1. Run `npx repomix` to generate `repomix-output.xml`
714: 2. Provide the file to an AI agent for full project context
715: 3. The AI gets a complete, token-efficient project snapshot
716: 4. Reference specific files by path when asking questions
717: 
718: **Note:** The `repomix-output.xml` is already generated and available in the project root.
