721: 
722: ## Query Performance Rules — Target: <50ms per Prisma query event
723: 
724: ### Verified Current State
725: - Prisma singleton is already globalThis-cached in `apps/backend/src/app/shared/prisma.ts`. Do not rewrite it as a plain module-level `new PrismaClient`.
726: - Adapter is `@prisma/adapter-pg` (node-postgres TCP pooling). DO NOT switch back to `@prisma/adapter-ppg` (HTTP-based, no keep-alive, 1500-2500ms per query from Bangladesh to US East).
727: - `PaperChunk.embedding` is enabled via `Unsupported("vector")`. HNSW index is created via migration.
728: - There are two `paper.service.ts` files. Active file is `apps/backend/src/app/modules/papers/paper.service.ts` (imported by `paper.controller.ts`).
729: - `@prisma/sqlcommenter-query-insights` is installed and wired into the singleton for Query Insights attribution.
730: - `prisma/seed.js` was modified to import `PrismaPg` adapter + generated client instead of raw `@prisma/client` (Prisma 7 requires adapter for client instantiation).
731: 
732: ### Terminal Query-Time Visibility
733: - The singleton registers a Prisma `$on('query')` listener in development.
734: - Any query event over 50ms is logged to the terminal as:
735:   `[SLOW QUERY] {duration}ms | {query first 150 chars} | params: {params first 80 chars}`
736: - This logging is the primary measurement tool — do not remove it.
737: - After each optimization, restart the backend and hit the affected endpoints; watch the terminal for slow-query warnings before/after.
738: 
739: ### Select Discipline
740: - All list queries must use explicit `select`.
741: - Never fetch `embedding` or binary file content in list views.
742: - PaperChunk list views select `id, content, page, idx, paperId` only.
743: 
744: ### Relation Loading
745: - Add `relationLoadStrategy: 'join'` only to `findMany` calls. It is invalid on `findFirst`, `create`, `update`, `upsert`.
746: - Keep explicit `select` inside every `include`.
747: 
748: ### Pagination
749: - Cursor-based pagination for papers, search, workspaces, notifications, and activity logs.
750: - Keep offset pagination only where `skip` is bounded by a small constant (e.g., cursor exclusion `skip: 1`).
751: 
752: ### Indexes
753: - New indexes use `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF NOT EXISTS`.
754: - Verify exact table/column case against `schema.prisma`.
755: - HNSW vector index uses `vector_cosine_ops` with `m = 16, ef_construction = 64`.
756: 
757: ### Version Alignment
758: - Keep `@prisma/client`, `prisma`, and `@prisma/adapter-*` on the same minor version.
759: 
760: ### Verification Workflow
761: 1. Apply one optimization at a time.
762: 2. Restart `yarn dev:backend`.
763: 3. Hit the affected endpoint(s) from the frontend or with `curl`.
764: 4. Check the terminal for `[SLOW QUERY]` output.
765: 5. Confirm duration dropped below 50ms before moving to the next fix.
766: 6. Run `yarn type-check` and `yarn lint` after each significant change.
767: 
768: ---
769: 
770: ## Database — ONE shared cloud DB (local dev + production)
771: 
772: ### Database Setup
773: - **Single Prisma Postgres (Prisma Cloud) database is used for BOTH local
774:   development and production.** There is NO local database. No WSL
775:   PostgreSQL. `docker` is not used.
776: - `DATABASE_URL` = Accelerate endpoint in `.env` (runtime queries via proxy)
777: - `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` = Direct PostgreSQL URL for migrations and adapter
778: - Both `.env` (local) and `.env.production` (deployed) point at the SAME
779:   cloud database — any local `yarn dev:backend` reads/writes production data.
780: 
781: ### Environment Strategy
782: - `.env` → same cloud DB (Accelerate URL + direct URL)
783: - `.env.production` → same cloud DB (deployed backend)
784: - The PG adapter picks up `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` from whichever `.env` is loaded
785: - Never commit `.env` or `.env.production` (already in `.gitignore`)
786: 
787: ### Migration Discipline
788: - ALWAYS use migrations — never `prisma db push`
789: - `prisma.config.ts` uses `DATABASE_URL` for migration, `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` for directUrl
790: - Run `yarn db:generate --sql` after every migration
791: - `prisma migrate dev` needs a shadow database; if shadow replay fails due to
792:   history drift (see below), fall back to writing the migration SQL by hand
793:   into `prisma/migrations/<timestamp>_<name>/migration.sql`, then
794:   `yarn prisma migrate deploy` (deploy does NOT use a shadow DB and only runs
795:   pending migrations).
796: 
797: ### Migration Drift (learned the hard way)
798: The schema in `schema.prisma` has accumulated columns and tables that were
799: added to the shared database via `prisma db push` (bypassing migration
800: history). This makes `prisma migrate dev` fail ("relation ... does not
801: exist" while replaying history in the shadow DB). Detection: run `migrate
802: dev --create-only` and read the error; or compare live columns against the
803: schema with psql against the DIRECT_DATABASE_URL. Fix options:
804: 1. **Best for additive changes (tables/columns that don't exist yet):**
805:    write the migration SQL by hand and `prisma migrate deploy`.
806: 2. For reconciliations: `prisma migrate dev --create-only --name
807:    reconcile_schema_drift` against a drift-free scratch DB, review the
808:    generated SQL carefully (may contain destructive ops), then `migrate
809:    deploy`.
810: 
811: ### Adapter Configuration
812: - Adapter: `@prisma/adapter-pg` with `pg` driver (TCP connection pooling)
813: - Connection: passes `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` to adapter
814: - Works with any standard `postgres://` URL (cloud or any provider)
815: - Pooling: `pg` driver pools TCP connections natively (no extra config needed)
816: - DO NOT use `@prisma/adapter-ppg` — no HTTP keep-alive, 1500ms+ per query with cloud DB latency from Bangladesh
817: 
818: ### Seed Script
819: - Location: `apps/backend/prisma/seed.js` (CommonJS)
820: - Script: `yarn db:seed` → runs `ts-node prisma/seed.js`
821: - Uses `@prisma/adapter-pg` with `PrismaPg` adapter (imported from generated client)
822: - Default password for all demo users: `password123`
823: - Demo users: admin@scholarflow.com, researcher@scholarflow.com, pro.researcher@scholarflow.com, teamlead@scholarflow.com
824: - Seeds the SHARED cloud DB — `.env` must have cloud `DATABASE_URL` +
825:   `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` (it does by default). Never seed against a scratch
826:   DB and expect data to appear locally.
827: - **Plan catalog (learned the hard way):** the checkout webhook resolves plans by
828:   `stripePriceId` then code `{tier}_{interval}`. `seed.js` creates only
829:   free/pro/institutional (no price IDs) — running it leaves the DB without
830:   pro_monthly/team_* rows and EVERY checkout webhook fails with
831:   "Plan not found" (user charged, no role granted). Run
832:   `seedPlans.js` too: `yarn ts-node prisma/seedPlans.js` with
833:   STRIPE_PRICE_* env vars set — it now uses the PrismaPg adapter like seed.js.
834:   The 2026-08-09 incident: user's Pro trial was never granted for exactly this.
835: 
836: ### Performance Verification Workflow
837: 1. Start backend: `yarn dev:backend` (connects to the shared cloud DB)
838: 2. Hit any DB endpoint from dashboard or curl
839: 3. Terminal shows `[SLOW QUERY] {duration}ms` for any query >50ms
840: 4. From Bangladesh against US-East cloud DB: expect 100-250ms per query
841:    (network-bound); on the deployed US-East backend: expect <50ms
842: 5. If a query is slow even on the deployed backend, check for missing
843:    indexes or N+1 queries
